files.docs/browser-tools.md:
# Browser tools

The page is app/index.html. browser-run SCENARIO_JSON OUTPUT_DIR runs locally supplied Chromium and Playwright, serves project files, returns action observations and writes captures to OUTPUT_DIR. No package download is needed.

A scenario has page, viewport and steps. Example actions:
- {"action":"click","selector":"button"}
- {"action":"fill","selector":"textarea","value":"Text"}
- {"action":"press","selector":"button","key":"End"}
- {"action":"resize","width":390,"height":420}
- {"action":"evaluate","script":"document.querySelector('main').innerText"}
- {"action":"capture","name":"agenda"}

A capture includes a PNG and rendered element bounds, styles, text and visibility. Local storage persists across actions and page reloads in a browser session.

